---
/**
 * ASSESSMENT & SUPPORT · MENTORING — audit 2.D6.
 *
 * ⚠ THE SCHOOL PUBLISHES ONE LINE OF MENTORING COPY. What it also publishes,
 * and what the stub missed, is its own recruitment advertising — and a school's
 * job adverts are a harder statement of what it staffs than any pastoral
 * paragraph. Sunbeam has advertised, in its own posters:
 *
 *   "clinical psychology counsellor and wellness trainer" (vacancies poster)
 *   "School counsellor: MA in counselling or clinical psychology with two years
 *    of experience as a school counsellor" (walk-in interview poster)
 *
 * A school that requires a master's degree and two years' experience for its
 * counsellor is describing its pastoral provision more precisely than a page of
 * copy could. Both lines are read off the posters in assets/jobs/.
 *
 * ═══ ALSO VERIFIED ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *   BCS Counsellors — "trained counsellors available to students"
 *     (data/facilities.ts, listed on campus).
 *
 * ⚠ NOT USED: data/campus.ts carries a "Counselling" entry marked
 * `verified: false`. It is not cited here.
 *
 * ⚠ NOT CLAIMED: a mentor-to-student ratio, a programme name, a meeting
 * frequency, how a mentor is assigned, or how a parent contacts one. None of it
 * is published, and inventing any of it would be inventing pastoral care.
 *
 * Composition: statement (ivory) → collage (sand, LEFT, what the school staffs
 * for) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcStatement from '../../../components/academics/system/AcStatement.astro';
import AcCollage from '../../../components/academics/system/AcCollage.astro';
import AcClose from '../../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/photos/sunbeem-5.jpg';
import pLib from '../../../assets/photos/sb-library.jpg';
import pCorridor from '../../../assets/corridor and stairs/DSC_1222 copy.jpg';
import pBench from '../../../assets/photos/sb-chem-lab.jpg';
import pCohort from '../../../assets/photos/sunbeem-3.jpg';

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mentoring — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="Mentoring at Sunbeam School Ballia: every student has a member of staff who knows them, with trained BCS counsellors on campus and a school counsellor post advertised at master's level."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Mentoring"
    standfirst="What a school staffs for says more than what it says about itself."
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' },
      { label: 'Assessment & Support', href: '/academics/assessment/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="Student council office-bearers and NCC cadets of Sunbeam School Ballia on stage with the school's dignitaries."
    position="50% 38%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcStatement
      ground="ivory"
      ghost="1:1"
      ghostAt="right"
      kicker="What the school publishes"
      statement="Someone who knows<br /><em>the child.</em>"
      body={[
        'Sunbeam states one thing about mentoring: that every student has <strong>a member of staff who knows them as a person rather than as a name on a class list</strong>. It is a single line, and it is not expanded here into a programme that has not been described.',
        'What that line is for is easy to say without inventing anything. A subject teacher seeing a child four times a week may not notice a change in them. Someone who already knows the child does — and the years in which a student is least likely to raise a problem themselves are exactly the years in which that difference matters.',
      ]}
    />

    <AcCollage
      ground="sand"
      side="left"
      kicker="And what it hires for"
      heading="A master’s degree,<br /><em>and two years of it</em>"
      body={[
        'The firmer evidence is in the school’s own recruitment posters, where a school states what it will and will not accept. Sunbeam’s walk-in advertisement sets its counsellor requirement in one line: <strong>“MA in counselling or clinical psychology with two years of experience as a school counsellor.”</strong>',
        'A separate vacancies poster lists a <strong>clinical psychology counsellor and wellness trainer</strong> among the posts it was recruiting to. Alongside those, the school lists <strong>BCS Counsellors</strong> — trained counsellors available to students — among its campus provision.',
      ]}
      ledger={[
        { k: 'Every student', v: 'A member of staff who knows them as a person, not as a row on a class list.' },
        { k: 'School counsellor', v: 'Advertised at MA in counselling or clinical psychology, with two years’ school experience.' },
        { k: 'Clinical psychology counsellor', v: 'Listed with a wellness trainer among the school’s advertised posts.' },
        { k: 'BCS Counsellors', v: 'Trained counsellors available to students, on campus.' },
      ]}
      lead={{ src: pLib, alt: `Students of ${school} reading at the long tables of the library, a member of staff at the head of the row` }}
      support={[
        { src: pCorridor, alt: `A corridor at ${school}, its classroom doors running the length of the block` },
        { src: pBench, alt: `Students of ${school} working along the chemistry bench` },
      ]}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="Noticed before<br /><em>it is a result.</em>"
      body="The school publishes that every student has a mentor, and its own adverts show what it requires of a counsellor. It does not publish a ratio, a programme name, a meeting frequency, or how a parent reaches a child's mentor."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Students and staff of ${school} gathered on the hall stage`}
      position="50% 42%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
